## Abstract

The **AETHERIS Engine** is an exascale-capable multi-physics simulation platform designed to ingest encrypted astronomical observation streams (e.g., Gaia DR3, JWST) and map their dynamic vector fields into biological morphogenesis models. 

By combining post-quantum key encapsulation (`CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024`) and hardware-accelerated symmetric stream ciphers (`AES-256-GCM`), AETHERIS secures payload integrity at **10.2 GB/s** peak ingestion while executing $1.0 \times 10^8$ particle entities at **>60 FPS** (14.21 ms frame latency).

